# Normalizes line endings so a Windows checkout (this project is edited
# from a OneDrive-synced folder on Windows) doesn't turn every text file
# into a diff of CRLF vs. the repo's LF the moment it's opened and saved.
# `eol=lf` forces LF in the working tree on every platform, not just what
# gets committed, so this fixes it for any fresh clone too, not just this
# one. Existing already-committed files won't be rewritten just by adding
# this file - see the renormalize step below.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files some tooling might add later - never touched by line-ending
# normalization regardless of what `text=auto` would otherwise guess.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.svg binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
*.pptx binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
